{% if not (HIDE_ARTIFACT_SUBMISSION_GUIDANCE|default(false)) %}
ARTIFACT SUBMISSION:
- Use {{SUBMIT_MD_ARTIFACT_TOOL_REFERENCE}} to submit an artifact: pass `artifact_type` and `content` (the complete markdown document per its `.agent/artifact-formats/<type>.md` format doc)
{% if VERIFY_MD_ARTIFACT_TOOL_NAME %}- Use {{VERIFY_MD_ARTIFACT_TOOL_REFERENCE}} to validate an artifact document without persisting it (read-only; same arguments; returns line/section/rule-anchored diagnostics){% endif %}
{% if STAGE_MD_ARTIFACT_TOOL_NAME %}- For long documents, stage incrementally: {{STAGE_MD_ARTIFACT_TOOL_REFERENCE}} appends (or `mode="replace_all"` replaces) draft content{% if GET_MD_DRAFT_TOOL_NAME %}, {{GET_MD_DRAFT_TOOL_REFERENCE}} returns the draft with diagnostics{% endif %}{% if FINALIZE_MD_ARTIFACT_TOOL_NAME %}, {{FINALIZE_MD_ARTIFACT_TOOL_REFERENCE}} validates and submits the assembled draft (the draft is retained either way){% endif %}{% if DISCARD_MD_DRAFT_TOOL_NAME %}, {{DISCARD_MD_DRAFT_TOOL_REFERENCE}} drops the draft for a genuine wholesale restart only — never to recover from validation errors or to make a revision substantially similar to the draft, which throws the document away and forces a full retype{% endif %}{% endif %}
{% if EDIT_MD_ARTIFACT_TOOL_NAME %}- Every submission stages its document as that artifact's draft, valid or not. To fix validation errors, edit the draft in place with {{EDIT_MD_ARTIFACT_TOOL_REFERENCE}}: pass `artifact_type` and `edits` (a list of `oldText`/`newText` pairs applied by sequential first-occurrence replacement, all-or-nothing if any `oldText` is missing). Use `dry_run` to preview the diff. Do NOT resend the whole document to change part of it.
- {{EDIT_MD_ARTIFACT_TOOL_REFERENCE}} IS a submission: it is {{SUBMIT_MD_ARTIFACT_TOOL_REFERENCE}} starting from the existing draft, and it submits the artifact canonically as soon as the edited draft validates — no separate {{FINALIZE_MD_ARTIFACT_TOOL_REFERENCE}} call. If the edited draft still has errors it is kept as a draft for further repair and nothing is submitted; the response reports `submitted` either way. Submitting does not end the phase, so a later edit in the same attempt simply resubmits.
- To revise a submitted or staged document: inspect it with {{GET_MD_DRAFT_TOOL_REFERENCE}}, then apply {{EDIT_MD_ARTIFACT_TOOL_REFERENCE}} edits. Replacing the whole document via {{STAGE_MD_ARTIFACT_TOOL_REFERENCE}} (`mode="replace_all"`) is the fallback when a rewrite really is wholesale — not for a revision whose content is substantially similar to the draft.
{% else %}- To revise a staged plan, call {{STAGE_MD_ARTIFACT_TOOL_REFERENCE}} (`mode="replace_all"`) with the complete updated document, inspect with {{GET_MD_DRAFT_TOOL_REFERENCE}}, then submit with {{FINALIZE_MD_ARTIFACT_TOOL_REFERENCE}}.
{% endif %}{% endif %}
- Use {{DECLARE_COMPLETE_TOOL_REFERENCE}} when finished
